 "notes": "Observed 95% upper limit (orange 'Experiment' curve) from Fig. 5 (exp_MC_ulims.eps in the e-print), extracted from the vector paths of the figure with axis calibration from major tick marks (verified: green MC-median minimum reproduces the quoted 2.4e-10 GeV^-1 at 0.36 Hz; top mass axis confirms m=h*f). The paper's limit is set at ~8 million frequencies from 0.01 to 10 Hz and plotted as a dense noisy band; reported points are the median of the plotted curve in 90 log-spaced frequency bins, which smooths over narrow strong/weak excursions (including the near-integer-Hz noise peaks the paper attributes to non-axion artifacts, Sec. VI). Paper defines L = g_aNN Nbar gamma^mu gamma5 N d_mu a with g_aNN in GeV^-1 (Eq. 1) / H = g_aNN grad(a).sigma_N (Eq. 2); converted to canonical dimensionless g_an = 2 m_n g_aNN with m_n = 0.93957 GeV. Mass converted from frequency via m_a = h f. Assumes axions are all of the local DM with rho = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Catena & Ullio).",
